camchrome: two persona coherence fixes the validator sweep found.

1. Schema 1 heap. Schema 1 reports the fleet-constant jsHeapSizeLimit (4,395,630,592), which is
   what V8 gives any machine with 8 GB or more. On a persona with less deviceMemory it is a heap
   no real machine of that class can have: V8 sizes the heap from physical memory, so 4 GB tops
   out near 4.05 GB. 89 of 500 Windows/Linux seeds had it (validator heap.exceeds_ram). Those
   personas now get the RAM-derived limit schema 2 already uses; everything at 8 GB and above,
   and any plausible imported limit, is unchanged.

2. WebGPU texture limits on mobile GPUs. The desktop WebGPU table (maxTextureDimension1D/2D
   16384) was served next to an Android GPU's WebGL MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE 8192, a pair no device
   reports (about 1 in 5 Android seeds; validator webgpu.texture2d_eq_webgl). The WebGPU 1D/2D
   limits are clamped down to the persona's WebGL limit. Downward only, so a capture's own lower
   value stays, and 967 still clamps against the host.

Validator after the change: 500 seeds x {unset, windows, macos, linux, android} x {schema 1, 2},
0 errors and 0 warnings (was 0 errors, 468 warnings).

--- a/components/ungoogled/persona_profile.cc
+++ b/components/ungoogled/persona_profile.cc
@@ -1378,6 +1378,28 @@
   // sentinel and is left alone.
   if (p.persona_schema >= 2 && p.js_heap_size_limit == 0)
     p.js_heap_size_limit = PersonaHeapLimitBytes(p);
+  // camchrome (998): schema 1 keeps the fleet-constant heap (persona_profile.h), which is what
+  // V8 reports on any machine with 8 GB or more. Below that it is a heap no real machine of
+  // the claimed deviceMemory can have (V8 sizes the heap from physical memory; 4 GB tops out
+  // near 4.05 GB), so those personas get the RAM-derived limit schema 2 uses. Personas at 8 GB
+  // and above, and any plausible imported limit, are unchanged.
+  if (p.persona_schema < 2 && p.js_heap_size_limit != 0) {
+    uint64_t heap_lo = 0, heap_hi = 0;
+    PersonaHeapLimitBounds(p, &heap_lo, &heap_hi);
+    if (p.js_heap_size_limit > heap_hi)
+      p.js_heap_size_limit = PersonaHeapLimitBytes(p);
+  }
+  // camchrome (998): a GPU's WebGPU 1D/2D texture limit is its GL MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE; the
+  // desktop WebGPU table (16384) next to a mobile GPU's 8192 WebGL limit was a pair no device
+  // reports. Clamp downward only, so a capture's own lower value stays.
+  if (!p.webgl_real && p.webgl_max_texture_size > 0) {
+    for (const char* key : {"maxTextureDimension1D", "maxTextureDimension2D"}) {
+      auto it = p.webgpu_limits.find(key);
+      if (it != p.webgpu_limits.end() &&
+          it->second > static_cast<uint64_t>(p.webgl_max_texture_size))
+        it->second = static_cast<uint64_t>(p.webgl_max_texture_size);
+    }
+  }
   // clearcote: WebGPU features for the model the FINAL renderer string names (seed, profile or
   // switch), unless a capture already supplied its own list or the GPU is real. Unknown models
   // leave the list empty and the real adapter's features are served.
